or;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="265.7" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><line x1="343.2" y1="242" x2="343.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="343.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="29" y1="242" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="29" y1="190" x2="33" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.4</text><line x1="29" y1="138" x2="33" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="138" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.8</text><line x1="29" y1="86" x2="33" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.2</text><line x1="29" y1="34" x2="33" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.6</text><text x="207.5" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">f / 10¹⁴ Hz</text><text x="29" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Ek(max) / eV</text><line x1="261.7" y1="186" x2="269.7" y2="194" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="261.7" y1="194" x2="269.7" y2="186" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="339.2" y1="78.1" x2="347.2" y2="86.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="339.2" y1="86.1" x2="347.2" y2="78.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="265.7,190 343.2,82.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/></svg>', 'Graph of maximum kinetic energy against frequency with two measured points, (6.0 × 10¹⁴ Hz, 0.40 eV) and (8.0 × 10¹⁴ Hz, 1.23 eV), joined by a straight line.'),
('cbe99897-cbd9-5671-8094-18d3ff1d1639', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 38, 38, 'Light of wavelength 420 nm gives a stopping potential of 1.20 V. Calculate the work function of the surface in eV. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.76', 'eV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'hf = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (420 × 10⁻⁹ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.960 eV. Φ = 2.960 − 1.20 = 1.76 eV. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: photon energy. C1: Φ = hf − eV_s. A1: Φ = 1.76 eV.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('227cd3ee-ebdf-5192-bd9a-1532668aeb20', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 39, 39, 'The same ultraviolet light falls on two metals, P with work function 2.0 eV and Q with 4.0 eV. Which statement is correct?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Electrons from P have the larger maximum kinetic energy', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Ek(max) = hf − Φ is larger for the smaller Φ. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: same hf. C1: smaller Φ larger Ek. A1: D (Electrons from P have the larger maximum kinetic energy).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('b254ed49-9762-5b81-a72c-2843d246f30f', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 40, 40, 'Light of wavelength 400 nm and power 5.0 mW falls on a sodium cathode (work function 2.28 eV). One photon in 500 releases an electron. (a) Calculate the photon energy in eV. (b) Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons. (c) Calculate the photocurrent when all emitted electrons are collected. Give only the answer to (c), in µA. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.218 uA', 'µA', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 3.108 eV. (b) 3.108 − 2.28 = 0.828 eV. (c) Photons per second = 5.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 4.972 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.006 × 10¹⁶; electrons = ÷ 500; I = 1.006 × 10¹⁶ ÷ 500 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.218 × 10⁻⁶ A. In µA: 3.218 × 10⁻⁶ × 10⁶ = 3.22. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: photon energy. C1: Ek(max). C1: photon rate. C1: I = ne. A1: I = 3.22 µA.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4b0e815c-t fg4b0e815c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4b0e815c-t">Sodium photocell</title><desc id="fg4b0e815c-d">A photocell with a sodium cathode lit by light of wavelength 400 nm and power 5.0 mW; the anode is held positive by a cell and the photocurrent is read on a microammeter.</desc><circle cx="175" cy="104" r="56" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M150,74 A40,40 0 0,0 150,134" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205" y1="92" x2="205" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="128" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">cathode</text><text x="205" y="132" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">anode</text><line x1="205" y1="14" x2="156" y2="76.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="153,80 154.6,73.2 159.2,76.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="222" y1="24" x2="158.4" y2="90.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="155,94 157.2,87.4 161.5,91.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="239" y1="34" x2="160.6" y2="104.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="157,108 159.7,101.6 163.7,105.9" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="246" y="16" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">400 nm, 5.0 mW</text><line x1="136.5" y1="104" x2="50" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205" y1="104" x2="310" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="104" x2="310" y2="152" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="176" x2="310" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="310" cy="164" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="310" y="164.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><text x="330" y="164" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">µA</text><line x1="50" y1="104" x2="50" y2="159" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="50" y1="169" x2="50" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="37" y1="169" x2="63" y2="169" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="43" y1="159" x2="57" y2="159" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="50" y1="224" x2="310" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A photocell with a sodium cathode lit by light of wavelength 400 nm and power 5.0 mW; the anode is held positive by a cell and the photocurrent is read on a microammeter.'),
('f9302505-49a1-50a6-89c6-c29031bfc168', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 41, 41, 'A student measures the maximum kinetic energy of photoelectrons for four frequencies: f = 6.0, 7.0, 8.0, 9.0 × 10¹⁴ Hz gives Ek(max) = 0.19, 0.60, 1.02, 1.43 eV. (a) Explain why a graph of Ek(max) against f should be a straight line. (b) Use the first and last points to find the gradient in eV per 10¹⁴ Hz. (c) Find the threshold frequency. Give only the answer to (c), in units of 10¹⁴ Hz.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.54', '10¹⁴ Hz', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Ek(max) = hf − Φ has the form y = mx + c. (b) Gradient = (1.43 − 0.19) ÷ (9.0 − 6.0) = 0.4133 eV per 10¹⁴ Hz, which is 4.133 × 10⁻¹⁵ eV Hz⁻¹. (c) Ek = 0 at f₀: f₀ = 6.0 × 10¹⁴ − 0.19 ÷ 4.133 × 10⁻¹⁵ = 5.54 × 10¹⁴ Hz. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: straight-line form. C1: gradient. M1: extrapolate to Ek = 0. C1: value. B1: gradient corresponds to h. A1: f₀ = 5.54 × 10¹⁴ Hz.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 316" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgecb3f197-t fgecb3f197-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgecb3f197-t">Photoelectron energies</title><desc id="fgecb3f197-d">Table and graph of the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons against the frequency of the light: four points lying on a straight line.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="37.7" y="8" width="324.5" height="56" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="37.7" y="8" width="324.5" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="96.6" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">f / 10¹⁴ Hz</text><text x="181.2" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">6.0</text><line x1="155.4" y1="8" x2="155.4" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="233" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">7.0</text><line x1="207.1" y1="8" x2="207.1" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="284.7" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">8.0</text><line x1="258.8" y1="8" x2="258.8" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="336.4" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">9.0</text><line x1="310.6" y1="8" x2="310.6" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="37.7" y1="36" x2="362.3" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="96.6" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Ek(max) / eV</text><text x="181.2" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.19</text><text x="233" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.60</text><text x="284.7" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.02</text><text x="336.4" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.43</text></g><g transform="translate(0,76)"><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="102.8" y1="34" x2="102.8" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="172.6" y1="34" x2="172.6" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="242.4" y1="34" x2="242.4" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="312.2" y1="34" x2="312.2" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="192" x2="382" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="152.5" x2="382" y2="152.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="113" x2="382" y2="113" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="73.5" x2="382" y2="73.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="192" x2="388" y2="192" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="192" x2="33" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,192 385.7,195 385.7,189" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="33,24 36,30.3 30.1,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="33" y1="192" x2="33" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="33" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">5</text><line x1="102.8" y1="192" x2="102.8" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="102.8" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><line x1="172.6" y1="192" x2="172.6" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="172.6" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">7</text><line x1="242.4" y1="192" x2="242.4" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="242.4" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="312.2" y1="192" x2="312.2" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="312.2" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">9</text><line x1="382" y1="192" x2="382" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="382" y="204" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="29" y1="192" x2="33" y2="192" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="192" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="29" y1="152.5" x2="33" y2="152.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="152.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.4</text><line x1="29" y1="113" x2="33" y2="113" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="113" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.8</text><line x1="29" y1="73.5" x2="33" y2="73.5" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="73.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.2</text><line x1="29" y1="34" x2="33" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.6</text><text x="207.5" y="224" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">f / 10¹⁴ Hz</text><text x="29" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">Ek(max) / eV</text><line x1="98.8" y1="169.2" x2="106.8" y2="177.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="98.8" y1="177.2" x2="106.8" y2="169.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="168.6" y1="128.8" x2="176.6" y2="136.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="168.6" y1="136.8" x2="176.6" y2="128.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.4" y1="87.3" x2="246.4" y2="95.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="238.4" y1="95.3" x2="246.4" y2="87.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="308.2" y1="46.8" x2="316.2" y2="54.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="308.2" y1="54.8" x2="316.2" y2="46.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons against the frequency of the light: four points lying on a straight line.'),
('fb4f8b48-ec18-5cb0-9dcd-4ca0e5b8129b', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 42, 42, 'Ultraviolet light of wavelength 200 nm falls on copper, work function 4.7 eV. (a) Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in eV. (b) Calculate their maximum momentum. (c) Calculate the de Broglie wavelength of the fastest photoelectrons, in nm. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹, e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.9974 nm', 'nm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) hf = 6.216 eV, Ek = 1.516 eV = 2.425 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. (b) p = √(2 × 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × 2.425 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6.647 × 10⁻²⁵ kg m s⁻¹. (c) λ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ ÷ 6.647 × 10⁻²⁵ = 9.974 × 10⁻¹⁰ m. In nm: 9.974 × 10⁻¹⁰ × 10⁹ = 0.997. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: Ek(max). C1: eV to J. C1: p = √(2mEk). C1: λ = h/p. A1: λ = 0.997 nm.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('7f69b7ed-3953-5dde-b270-68a194227008', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 43, 43, 'With light of wavelength 400 nm the stopping potential for a surface is 1.05 V; with 500 nm it is 0.43 V. (a) Write the photoelectric equation for each wavelength in terms of h, c, λ, e, V_s and Φ. (b) Subtract to eliminate Φ. (c) Calculate h. Give only the answer to (c), in units of 10⁻³⁴ J s. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.613', '10⁻³⁴ J s', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) hc/λ = Φ + eV_s for each. (b) hc(1/λ₁ − 1/λ₂) = e(V₁ − V₂). (c) h = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × (1.05 − 0.43) ÷ (3.00 × 10⁸ × (2.5 × 10⁶ − 2.0 × 10⁶)) = 6.61 × 10⁻³⁴ J s. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: two equations. M1: eliminate Φ. C1: 1/λ values. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: h = 6.61 × 10⁻³⁴ J s.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0f42599a-t fg0f42599a-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0f42599a-t">Measuring the stopping potential</title><desc id="fg0f42599a-d">A photocell connected to a variable supply that makes the anode negative, in series with a sensitive meter; the supply is raised until the current just falls to zero.</desc><circle cx="175" cy="104" r="56" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><path d="M150,74 A40,40 0 0,0 150,134" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205" y1="92" x2="205" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="128" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">cathode</text><text x="205" y="132" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">anode</text><line x1="205" y1="14" x2="156" y2="76.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="153,80 154.6,73.2 159.2,76.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="222" y1="24" x2="158.4" y2="90.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="155,94 157.2,87.4 161.5,91.5" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="239" y1="34" x2="160.6" y2="104.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="157,108 159.7,101.6 163.7,105.9" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="246" y="16" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">400 nm or 500 nm</text><line x1="136.5" y1="104" x2="50" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205" y1="104" x2="310" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="104" x2="310" y2="152" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="310" y1="176" x2="310" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="310" cy="164" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="310" y="164.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><line x1="50" y1="104" x2="50" y2="159" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="50" y1="169" x2="50" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="37" y1="159" x2="63" y2="159" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="43" y1="169" x2="57" y2="169" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="70" y="164" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">variable</text><line x1="50" y1="224" x2="310" y2="224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A photocell connected to a variable supply that makes the anode negative, in series with a sensitive meter; the supply is raised until the current just falls to zero.'),
('c16468fb-0340-58b8-ba34-0485f1e2945f', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 44, 44, 'A clean zinc plate (work function 4.3 eV) is lit first with ultraviolet of wavelength 250 nm and then with 300 nm. (a) Calculate the photon energy for each wavelength in eV. (b) State which wavelength releases electrons. (c) Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the electrons released, in eV. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6725', 'eV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 250 nm: 4.972 eV; 300 nm: 4.144 eV. (b) Only 250 nm, since 4.14 eV < 4.3 eV. (c) Ek = 4.972 − 4.3 = 0.672 eV. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: both photon energies. B1: comparison with Φ. M1: Ek = hf − Φ. C1: value. A1: Ek(max) = 0.672 eV.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('d480cf5e-4892-539b-817d-40aa9d294e23', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 45, 45, 'Light of frequency 1.5 × 10¹⁵ Hz falls on a metal of work function 4.2 eV. (a) Calculate the photon energy in eV. (b) Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in joules. (c) Calculate their maximum speed. Give only the answer to (c), in units of 10⁵ m s⁻¹. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8.414', '10⁵ m s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 1.5 × 10¹⁵ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 6.216 eV. (b) Ek = (6.216 − 4.2) × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.225 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. (c) v = √(2 × 3.225 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 8.41 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: photon energy. C1: Ek in eV. C1: eV to J. M1: ½mv² = Ek. C1: value. A1: v = 8.41 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('4a98be1a-e100-5832-915f-737666adac37', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 46, 46, 'In a wave model, light of intensity 1.0 × 10⁻³ W m⁻² falls on a metal of work function 2.3 eV, and each electron can collect energy only from an area of about 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ m². (a) Calculate the power reaching this area. (b) Calculate the time needed to collect 2.3 eV. (c) Explain how this conflicts with experiment. Give only the answer to (b), in s. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3680', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P = 1.0 × 10⁻³ × 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 1.0 × 10⁻²² W. (b) t = 2.3 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻²² = 3680 s. (c) Emission is observed immediately, even at low intensity, because the energy comes in photons. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: P = IA. C1: Φ in J. M1: t = E/P. C1: value. B1: no delay observed. A1: t = 3680 s.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('39eb7992-2fba-5b21-8b74-e3c1f3fe484b', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 47, 47, 'An isolated metal sphere (work function 4.5 eV) is lit by ultraviolet of wavelength 200 nm. As electrons leave, the sphere becomes positively charged. (a) Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in eV. (b) Explain why emission eventually stops. (c) Calculate the potential of the sphere when emission stops. Give only the answer to (c). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.716', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 6.216 − 4.5 = 1.716 eV. (b) The positive sphere attracts the electrons back; once its potential equals the stopping potential none escape. (c) V = 6.216 − 4.5 = 1.72 V. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: photon energy. C1: Ek(max). B1: attraction back. C1: V = Ek/e. A1: V = 1.72 V.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('a9730163-dc9a-5290-a2d4-10fd1714ab43', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 48, 48, 'Light of wavelength 300 nm and then 250 nm falls on a metal of work function 3.6 eV. (a) Calculate Ek(max) for each wavelength in eV. (b) Calculate (maximum speed with 250 nm) ÷ (maximum speed with 300 nm). Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.589', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 300 nm: 4.144 − 3.6 = 0.5437 eV; 250 nm: 4.972 − 3.6 = 1.372 eV. (b) v ∝ √Ek: ratio = √(1.372 ÷ 0.5437) = 1.59. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: both photon energies. C1: both Ek(max). M1: v ∝ √Ek. C1: ratio. A1: ratio = 1.59.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('673f152a-dad3-5ff0-9ed8-50ec3cfdf696', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 49, 49, 'Light of wavelength 420 nm and power 0.10 mW falls on a photocell, which gives a current of 0.60 µA. (a) Calculate the number of photons arriving per second. (b) Calculate the number of electrons emitted per second. (c) Calculate the percentage of photons that release an electron. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.776', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ 420 × 10⁻⁹ = 4.736 × 10⁻¹⁹ J; n = 1.0 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 4.736 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 2.112 × 10¹⁴ s⁻¹. (b) 0.60 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.750 × 10¹² s⁻¹. (c) 3.750 × 10¹² ÷ 2.112 × 10¹⁴ × 100 = 1.78 %. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: photon energy. C1: photon rate. C1: electron rate. M1: ratio × 100. C1: value. A1: efficiency = 1.78%.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('edf73ca8-8de7-500b-8373-e47cc3455698', '7d22edfc-44c4-4846-9769-292936cb7827', '7b93970a-92bd-55df-bca6-9d3907e1c231', 'a-level', '28.3', '9702 coursebook 28.3 · The photoelectric effect', 50, 50, 'A metal has a threshold wavelength of 540 nm. (a) Calculate its work function in eV. (b) Light of wavelength 400 nm falls on it. Calculate the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons in eV. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.8057', 'eV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Φ = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (540 × 10⁻⁹ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.302 eV. (b) hf = 3.108 eV, so Ek = 3.108 − 2.302 = 0.806 eV. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: Φ = hc/λ₀. C1: photon energy. M1: Ek = hf − Φ. C1: value. A1: Ek(max) = 0.806 eV.', 5, NULL, NULL)
INSERT INTO problem_options (id, problem_id, option_text, option_letter, is_correct, "order") VALUES
('ac9f87fd-32d9-53e6-be2e-ce3be585b33b', 'dd7d5694-644a-5bac-9812-4d1bf1e1502f', 'The energy of the photons that fall on the metal', 'A', false, 0),
